%N A398159 Numbers k such that sigma(k) = psi(k) + Omega(k)^5.
%C A398159 The sequence is infinite because it contains all numbers of the form 7 * 127 * p^2, where p is any prime such that gcd(p, 7 * 127) = 1.
%e A398159 3556 is a term since sigma(3556) = 7168 = 6144 + 4^5 = psi(3556) + Omega(3556)^5.
%o A398159 (PARI) isok(k) = {my(f = factor(k)); sigma(f) == prod(i=1, #f~, (f[i, 1]+1) * f[i, 1]^(f[i, 2]-1)) + bigomega(f)^5; } \\ _Amiram Eldar_, Jul 22 2026
%Y A398159 Cf. A244963 (sigma minus psi), A001222 (Omega), A390253, A397843.
%K A398159 nonn,new
%O A398159 1,2
%A A398159 _S. I. Dimitrov_, Jul 22 2026
